        "text": "The growth of the NFT market and the large amounts of money that began exchanging hands also pushed the development of GameFi. How do players get rewarded in GameFi? In GameFi, the reward can come in different forms, such as cryptocurrencies or in game assets like virtual land, avatars, weapons, and costumes. Each GameFi project will adopt a different model and game economy. In most cases, the in game assets are NFTs residing on the blockchain, meaning they can be traded on NFT marketplaces. In other cases, however, the in game assets must be converted into NFTs before players can trade or sell them. Typically, the in game assets also provide specific benefits to the players, allowing them to earn more rewards. But some games also feature collectibles, avatars, and cosmetics that are purely visual items and have no impact on the gameplay.",
